  "description": "The bot will identify itself as **BotMaster** and run under the standard **/bin/bash** shell. Its core functionality is extended by three plugins\u2014**logger**, **auth**, and **monitor**\u2014and it is configured to stay active for a time\u2011to\u2011live of **3600 seconds** (one hour) before needing a restart.\n\nTwo deployment strategies are defined. The **default** strategy connects with the JID **user@example.com**, pulling its password from the **BOT_PASSWORD** environment variable. It is set to interact with the users **alice@example.com** and **bob@example.com**, and will join the conference rooms **room1@conference.example.com** and **room2@conference.example.com**. The **dev** strategy uses the JID **devuser@example.org**, with its password sourced from **DEV_BOT_PASSWORD**; it has no designated people contacts and will only join **devroom@conference.example.org**.",
  "reference_json": {
    "options": {
      "nick": "BotMaster",
      "plugins": [
        "logger",
        "auth",
        "monitor"
      ],
      "shell": "/bin/bash",
      "ttl": 3600
    },
    "strategies": {
      "default": {
        "jid": "user@example.com",
        "password_env": "BOT_PASSWORD",
        "people": [
          "alice@example.com",
          "bob@example.com"
        ],
        "rooms": [
          "room1@conference.example.com",
          "room2@conference.example.com"
        ]
      },
      "dev": {
        "jid": "devuser@example.org",
        "password_env": "DEV_BOT_PASSWORD",
        "people": [],
        "rooms": [
          "devroom@conference.example.org"
        ]
      }
    }
  }
}